cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite CASSIE and the Godot module it is vendored from.
title: CASSIE Godot module, curvenet subset (vendored)
abstract: >-
  83 of the 105 files under modules/cassie/src of the org's Godot fork
  (entities-godot), 596,233 bytes: the pen-to-curvenet-to-mesh path of the
  CASSIE sketching system (Yu et al., CHI 2021) as the fork ported it to
  Godot. Kept: sketcher, beautifier and its params, stroke packet,
  constraints, curve fit and RDP, the Eigen-free Track 5 solver with the
  CPU dispatchers for the curve_* and spmv kernels, the sketch graph and
  surface manager/patch pipeline, curvenet, knot, extractor, polar,
  triangulator, remesh, refine, polygon_triangulation and delaunay_geogram.
  Left out: cassie_path_3d, cassie_surface, intrinsic_triangulation,
  polygon_triangulation_godot, profile_mover, edge_collider, quad_mesh, the
  GPU dispatchers (cassie_mas_gpu, cassie_slang_gpu, saxpby_dispatch),
  lean_ffi, register_types, doc_classes and tests; and every prebuilt
  kernel (*.spv, *.cpu.cpp). tools/vendor/cassie_subset.sh reproduces the
  tree from the pinned commit and applies tools/vendor/patches/cassie.patch,
  which holds these local adaptations:
  (1) delaunay_geogram.{h,cpp} rewritten: delaunay_triangulate_2d_raw runs
  on GEO::Delaunay::create(2, "BDEL2d") in double, the input mapped into
  the unit box first, instead of Godot's Delaunay2D; the Godot-typed
  delaunay_triangulate_2d / delaunay_tetrahedralize_3d overloads are
  dropped (mwt's DMWT.cpp:548 is the only caller).
  (2) the four curve_* dispatchers and spmv_dispatch include the
  Lean-emitted kernels/cassie/cpp/<kernel>_emit.cpp inside a namespace,
  after the slang cpp prelude with its EXTERN_C macros emptied (the
  guest/avbd/avbd_cpu.cpp pattern), and call main_0_Thread instead of
  _main_0 from thirdparty/avbd/*.cpu.cpp. spmv_dispatch includes
  spmv_df32_emit.cpp, named after the Lean module it is emitted from
  (Cloth.SlangCodegen.SpmvDf32, kernels/cassie/kernels.txt), where
  entities-godot names it spmv.cpu.cpp. The emits' struct, field and
  entry names (CasteljauParams_0, GbParams_0, NewtonParams_0, RdpParams_0,
  SpmvDf32Params_0, GlobalParams_0.*_0, main_0_Thread) are those the
  dispatchers were written against: outside the prelude and #line
  directives the five emits match thirdparty/avbd/*.cpu.cpp line for line
  (gates/4-curvenet/kernel-parity.log).
  (3) CassieSurfacePatch::get_callback returns
  callable_mp(this, &CassieSurfacePatch::project) instead of the
  string-bound Callable(this, "project").
  (4) CassieSketcher gains split_closed_strokes (default true): a closed
  stroke enters the sketch graph as two half polylines through
  add_stroke_intersecting, so it bounds a two-edge cycle instead of a
  self-loop edge that yields no patch.
  (5) CassieSketchGraph::sample_cycle_boundary samples two-edge cycles
  (it refused N < 3) and, where both of an edge's ends are shared with the
  next edge, walks on from where the previous edge left off. Without it (4)
  never produced a patch: find_cycles reported the two-edge cycle and the
  surface manager got an empty boundary (Gate 4 pen_sphere: 1 cycle, 0
  patches).
